schemaVersion: 1
id: apartment-hunt-root
name: Apartment Hunt
kind: root
version: 0.1.0
description: An apartment scout for Israel. It asks what you need, then searches Yad2, Madlan and more twice a day and puts the places worth seeing on a map, with why each one fits.
entry: index.md
domain: Lifestyle

# The app this cabinet opens on. Older Cabinets open on index.md.
app: hunt

# Optional: everything here runs without it. References only: accounts never appear here.
connectors:
  - id: google-calendar
    need: better-with
    access: [create]
    why: Puts a viewing you booked on your calendar, when you ask.
    usedBy: [agents/apartment-scout]

# Things to try in this cabinet: at most 16, each at most 80 characters.
prompts:
  - text: "I am looking for an apartment. Ask me what you need to know."
  - text: "Search now and show me the best three."
  - text: "Is this listing a fair price? I will paste the link."
  - text: "Which neighbourhoods should I look at that I have not thought of?"
  - text: "What should I ask the landlord before I go to see it?"
  - text: "Write a short message to the owner of my top pick."
  - text: "What is a fair rent for 3 rooms where I am looking?"
  - text: "Read this lease and tell me what to push back on."
  - text: "How much can I afford to buy with my savings and salary?"
  - text: "Why did you pass on the places you passed on?"
  - text: "Change my search: I can go up to 500 more a month."
  - text: "Put my viewing on Thursday at 6 on my calendar."
    connector: google-calendar
